Contract limits / review decisions
- The six-word size tag does not prove DT-aware AUTO_ZRELADDR. On a non-128-MiB
  aligned RAM base, require the Linux v5.12+ algorithm (or verified backport),
  or a matching fixed ZRELADDR. Docs now make this explicit. No version-banner
  heuristic is claimed to prove the property at runtime.
- no-map subtraction respects the supplied tree's enabled no-map children and
  the mandatory equal root/reserved-memory cell widths plus ranges presence
  checked by Linux __reserved_mem_check_root. Parent status is ignored by the
  flat-DT scanner; the spin-table contract retains its stricter parent gate.
  Tests cover 1/2 cells, partial overlaps, disabled children, ignored malformed
  parent layouts, retained target header entries and live-only reservations.
- Whole-workspace kernel memsz zero-fill protects the relocated appended-DTB
  probe; unit tests seed stale FDT magic at that probe. QEMU confirms handoff,
  not arbitrary decompressor contracts or phone cache/coherency.
- Ambiguous/transient live reservations remain conservatively reserved.
- Higher zImage placement and broad shared-loader/FDT-parser refactors are
  deferred optimizations, not required to establish this bounded handoff.

